.TH UA1000GUI 1 "November 2026" "ua1000gui 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ua1000gui \- control panel for the UA-1000
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ua1000gui
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR file ]
.br
.B ua1000gui
.BR \-h | \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ua1000gui
shows and changes the settings of a Roland/EDIROL UA-1000 audio interface:
the INPUT MONITOR and OUTPUT MONITOR mixers, the MONITOR OUT level, the
front-panel switches and, from the
.B Device
menu, the patch bay, the memories and the USER SET (the power-on settings,
including the sample rate).
.PP
Faders move through the same 1023 positions as the vendor's panel and show
their value in dB; they respond to the keyboard and the scroll wheel.
.PP
When it connects, the panel asks the device for its settings and shows
them; it keeps them in the state file it shares with
.BR ua1000ctl (1),
with the solos and the memories it stored, which the device cannot report,
and follows changes that
.B ua1000ctl
makes while it is open.
If the device does not answer, the saved state is sent to it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR"
The ALSA rawmidi port; by default the port named
.B "UA-1000 Control"
is used.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-state " \fIfile\fR"
The state file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH MENU
.TP
.B Patch Bay\(fm
The routing tables and their presets.
.TP
.B Notes\(fm
A notepad for what is wired where, saved beside the state file.
.TP
.B Send All Settings
Send the whole state to the device.
.TP
.B Reconnect
Look for the device again.
.TP
.BR "Store Memory\(fm" ", " "Load Memory\(fm" ", " "Store USER SET\(fm"
The device's five memories and its power-on settings; offered only while
the device is connected.
.TP
.B Reset to Defaults\(fm
Every channel to 0 dB and on; OUTPUT 1\-10 and INPUT 9\-10 as linked stereo pairs (odd left, even right), INPUT 1\-8 centred; the panel and patch bay to their
initial settings.
.TP
.B Quit
Also Ctrl+Q.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ua1000/state
The editor's state, or
.I ~/.local/state/ua1000/state
when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is not set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ua1000ctl (1)
